https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135155452,imgsize-50506.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-American student terminated from campus news website after he voted for Democrat in Texas]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154640.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-american-student-who-announced-his-vote-against-anti-indian-bigotry-in-texas-claims-he-has-been-terminated-from-campus-reforms-program/articleshow/135154640.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-american-student-who-announced-his-vote-against-anti-indian-bigotry-in-texas-claims-he-has-been-terminated-from-campus-reforms-program/articleshow/135154640.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:52:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135154656,imgsize-37244.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[$38,000 to $40,000 per fake marriage: Fraud for Green Card busted]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135153489.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/38000-to-40000-per-fake-marriage-massive-fraud-ring-for-facilitating-green-card-busted-in-massachusetts-us-citizen-was-selling-american-dream-and-investing-money-in-dominican-republic/articleshow/135153489.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/38000-to-40000-per-fake-marriage-massive-fraud-ring-for-facilitating-green-card-busted-in-massachusetts-us-citizen-was-selling-american-dream-and-investing-money-in-dominican-republic/articleshow/135153489.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T23:58:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135153633,imgsize-47708.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rhode Island volunteers reused 600+ Christmas trees to restore riverbanks and protect young trout]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135152075.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an inspiring environmental effort, volunteers in Rhode Island gathered over 600 old Christmas trees for the 'Trees for Trout' initiative, aimed at restoring riverbanks. By bringing their discarded trees to designated collection sites at Arcadia Management Area, residents have made a significant contribution toward creating sustainable trout habitats and mitigating soil erosion. This project not only enhances local waterways but also promotes community involvement in ecological preservation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/rhode-island-collected-more-than-600-unwanted-christmas-trees-in-2026-but-instead-of-sending-them-to-landfills-volunteers-are-placing-them-along-damaged-streams-to-rebuild-riverbanks-and-shelter-young-trout/articleshow/135152075.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/rhode-island-collected-more-than-600-unwanted-christmas-trees-in-2026-but-instead-of-sending-them-to-landfills-volunteers-are-placing-them-along-damaged-streams-to-rebuild-riverbanks-and-shelter-young-trout/articleshow/135152075.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T23:09:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135152358,imgsize-1096870.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Portia gifted Ellen a Rwanda gorilla project in 2018; its campus welcomed 40,000+ visitors by 2023]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135151560.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Portia de Rossi gifted Ellen DeGeneres a conservation project which led to the Ellen DeGeneres Campus opening in Rwanda. The campus supports wildlife protection and offers educational opportunities for local students and communities. Since its opening, it has welcomed numerous visitors and hosted thousands of Rwandan schoolchildren for science lessons. The project emphasizes sustainable practices and aims to monitor and protect endangered mountain gorillas.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2018-portia-de-rossi-surprised-ellen-degeneres-with-a-gorilla-conservation-project-by-september-2023-its-rwanda-campus-had-welcomed-over-40000-visitors-including-more-than-7500-local-schoolchildren/articleshow/135151560.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2018-portia-de-rossi-surprised-ellen-degeneres-with-a-gorilla-conservation-project-by-september-2023-its-rwanda-campus-had-welcomed-over-40000-visitors-including-more-than-7500-local-schoolchildren/articleshow/135151560.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T22:51:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135151822,imgsize-873686.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US midterms 2026: Mark Carney rejects US claim of election interference, says 'no merit']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135151327.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/us-midterms-2026-mark-carney-rejects-us-claim-of-election-interference-says-no-merit/articleshow/135151327.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/us-midterms-2026-mark-carney-rejects-us-claim-of-election-interference-says-no-merit/articleshow/135151327.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T22:48:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135151716,imgsize-712104.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump says he will talk to Musk if Ukraine's Starlink issues persist]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135152041.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/i-will-get-it-straightened-out-trump-says-he-will-talk-to-musk-if-ukraines-starlink-issues-persist/articleshow/135152041.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/i-will-get-it-straightened-out-trump-says-he-will-talk-to-musk-if-ukraines-starlink-issues-persist/articleshow/135152041.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T23:16:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135152483,imgsize-56432.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Alicia Keys and Swizz Beatz bought a $20.8M California cliffside home in 2019]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135151251.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Alicia Keys and Swizz Beatz made a significant purchase in 2019, acquiring the Razor House in La Jolla for $20.8 million. This architectural masterpiece, designed by Wallace E. Cunningham, boasts panoramic Pacific Ocean views. The duo transformed this modern creation into a warm family abode, enriched with artworks from the Dean Collection, reflecting Swizz Beatz's dream of a creative hideaway and highlighting the prestige of California's architectural landscape.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2019-alicia-keys-and-swizz-beatz-paid-20-8-million-for-a-glass-walled-california-cliff-house-that-had-originally-been-offered-for-30-million-two-years-later-they-revealed-its-transformation-into-an-art-filled-family-retreat/articleshow/135151251.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2019-alicia-keys-and-swizz-beatz-paid-20-8-million-for-a-glass-walled-california-cliff-house-that-had-originally-been-offered-for-30-million-two-years-later-they-revealed-its-transformation-into-an-art-filled-family-retreat/articleshow/135151251.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T22:40:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135151509,imgsize-1025934.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Aspen Estate Sale Closes: Slack and Away founders net $5m gain; sale not linked to separation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135136095.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Stewart Butterfield and Jen Rubio recently finalized the sale of their Aspen estate for $30 million, right after their separation. They originally acquired the property for around $25 million in January 2021, yielding a nice profit despite initially aiming for $45 million. The estate has been purchased by David and Erika Sands, professional poker players, who now add it to their diverse real estate holdings across New York and California.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2021-slack-co-founder-stewart-butterfield-and-away-founder-jen-rubio-bought-a-five-acre-aspen-estate-for-25-million-after-listing-it-for-45-million-they-sold-the-property-for-30-million/articleshow/135136095.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2021-slack-co-founder-stewart-butterfield-and-away-founder-jen-rubio-bought-a-five-acre-aspen-estate-for-25-million-after-listing-it-for-45-million-they-sold-the-property-for-30-million/articleshow/135136095.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:57:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135136289,imgsize-1374673.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bob Barker’s historic Los Angeles mansion sells for $6.325 million after renovation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135120012.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A charming piece of Hollywood Hills history, the home once owned by Bob Barker has seen an impressive makeover. Julia Dempster, the interior designer, cleverly blended modern enhancements with the house's original charm, showcasing stunning stained-glass windows and wrought iron accents. Originally listed at over $8 million, it found a new owner, Randy Pitchford, for $6.325 million in spring 2026, further enriching his portfolio of Hollywood landmarks.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2024-interior-designers-paid-3-874-million-for-bob-barkers-historic-1929-los-angeles-mansion-after-an-extensive-renovation-the-5906-square-foot-home-sold-in-april-2026-for-6-325-million/articleshow/135120012.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2024-interior-designers-paid-3-874-million-for-bob-barkers-historic-1929-los-angeles-mansion-after-an-extensive-renovation-the-5906-square-foot-home-sold-in-april-2026-for-6-325-million/articleshow/135120012.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:52:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135120222,imgsize-152007.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lucy Hale's $2.95M LA home gets a colourful makeover after Sobriety]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135119913.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2019-lucy-hale-bought-a-1940s-spanish-style-home-in-los-angeles-for-2-95-million-after-getting-sober-in-2022-she-spent-three-years-transforming-it-into-a-colourful-retreat-with-a-meditation-room/articleshow/135119913.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2019-lucy-hale-bought-a-1940s-spanish-style-home-in-los-angeles-for-2-95-million-after-getting-sober-in-2022-she-spent-three-years-transforming-it-into-a-colourful-retreat-with-a-meditation-room/articleshow/135119913.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135120125,imgsize-669967.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jason Momoa’s water brand expands hotel refill machines after removing 6 million plastic bottles]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135119843.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Mananalu, founded by Jason Momoa, aims to eliminate single-use plastic bottles through innovative refill systems. The newly implemented technology connects to local water sources and fills reusable containers. This approach also significantly reduces carbon emissions associated with traditional bottled water. Initiatives are starting in Hawaii, where waste management is crucial due to heavy reliance on imported water.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/jason-momoa-launched-a-water-brand-to-fight-plastic-pollution-after-reporting-more-than-6-million-plastic-bottles-removed-his-company-introduced-hotel-machines-that-can-refill-up-to-500-bottles-an-hour/articleshow/135119843.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/jason-momoa-launched-a-water-brand-to-fight-plastic-pollution-after-reporting-more-than-6-million-plastic-bottles-removed-his-company-introduced-hotel-machines-that-can-refill-up-to-500-bottles-an-hour/articleshow/135119843.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T23:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135119964,imgsize-135902.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1890 Sherlock Holmes first edition found in charity shop sells for £11,520]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135117224.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A first-edition edition of The Sign of Four surfaced among the book donations at an Oxfam shop, piquing the interest of staff who recognized its rare value. After seeking expert appraisal, the book fetched an impressive £11,520 at Bonhams auction house. The funds raised will greatly benefit Oxfam's humanitarian efforts globally, highlighting how valuable donations can be when assessed properly.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-forgotten-1890-first-edition-of-sherlock-holmes-novel-the-sign-of-four-arrived-among-ordinary-charity-shop-donations-in-england-staff-spotted-its-significance-and-it-sold-for-11520/articleshow/135117224.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-forgotten-1890-first-edition-of-sherlock-holmes-novel-the-sign-of-four-arrived-among-ordinary-charity-shop-donations-in-england-staff-spotted-its-significance-and-it-sold-for-11520/articleshow/135117224.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T22:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135117411,imgsize-1419536.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US midterms 2026: Trump admin files lawsuit over Alaska Senate race, seeks to block results if GOP loses]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135150666.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/us-midterms-2026-trump-admin-files-lawsuit-over-alaska-senate-race-seeks-to-block-results-if-gop-loses/articleshow/135150666.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mid-term-elections/news/us-midterms-2026-trump-admin-files-lawsuit-over-alaska-senate-race-seeks-to-block-results-if-gop-loses/articleshow/135150666.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T22:04:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135150857,imgsize-1516189.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Butterflies Rebound After Restoration: Ex-wheat farm records 5,290 in 2026; rare species appear]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135140712.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Halnaker Hill Farm in West Sussex has experienced a remarkable surge in butterfly populations thanks to dedicated habitat restoration initiatives. In the spring of 2026, surveys noted 5,290 butterflies representing 28 different species, including some that are quite rare. This ecological project has fostered a rich variety of habitats that not only attract butterflies but also support bird life and other insects.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/after-40-years-of-wheat-farming-a-330-acre-stretch-of-land-in-england-was-turned-into-a-wildlife-haven-just-two-years-later-surveys-recorded-5290-butterflies-including-rare-species-never-previously-seen-in-the-fields/articleshow/135140712.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/after-40-years-of-wheat-farming-a-330-acre-stretch-of-land-in-england-was-turned-into-a-wildlife-haven-just-two-years-later-surveys-recorded-5290-butterflies-including-rare-species-never-previously-seen-in-the-fields/articleshow/135140712.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T21:52:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135140770,imgsize-876023.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2017, J.J. Watt donated $100K for Hurricane Harvey relief, raised $41.6M to help Texas flood victims]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135149832.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 2017, former NFL star J.J. Watt donated $100,000 to launch a fundraiser for Hurricane Harvey victims in Texas. Initially targeting $200,000, the campaign eventually raised $41.6 million by August 2018. The money helped rebuild more than 600 homes, restore over 420 childcare centres, distribute 26 million meals and provide healthcare to thousands.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2017-j-j-watt-donated-100000-to-hurricane-harvey-relief-launching-a-fundraiser-that-raised-41-6-million-to-help-texas-flood-victims-rebuild-over-600-homes-and-restore-more-than-420-childcare-centres/articleshow/135149832.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/